      "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"85c581f00291a772\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHome to the most westerly point on the British mainland, Corrachadh Mòr, Ardnamurchan is a scenic spot located in the beauty of the West Highlands Peninsula. It’s a great place to explore on two wheels, with cycle paths, trails and quiet roads, giving you the opportunity to explore this corner of Scotland at your own pace and in an eco-friendly way. Gaelic for ‘headland of the great seas’, Ardnamuchan boasts its famous lighthouse, a rocky northern coast, and is designated as a National Scenic Area due to its mesmerising scenery and landscape.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"85c581f00291a772\">>>",
